<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Marshal, 1st Earl of Pembroke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1146–<a href="/years/1219">1219</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as William Marshal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Marshal was an English knight who served four Angevin kings and became famous as a tournament champion. His marriage to the heiress Isabel de Clare in 1189 brought him Pembroke and the lordship of Leinster, where he founded towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-ross">New Ross</a>. From 1216 he was regent for the young Henry III.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-marshal-1st-earl-of-pembroke.jpg" alt="William Marshal, 1st Earl of Pembroke" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JvL · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Effigy_of_William_Marshall_-_52052671403.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
